{
  "info": {
    "name": "buzzd",
    "description": "HTTP endpoints of the buzzd server and a WebSocket guide.\n\n## WebSocket\n\nPostman doesn't save WebSocket requests in the collection JSON file, so they are created manually (once):\n\n1. **New → WebSocket**, URL: `{{wsUrl}}/ws?token={{token1}}` (player 1). Save it to this collection.\n2. Same for `{{token2}}` (player 2) and `{{token3}}` (spectator).\n3. In each WebSocket request, under **Saved messages**, save the messages below.\n\nOrder: run **Create room**, then the **Join** requests (they write tokens into the collection variables), then connect over WebSocket within 30 s.\n\n### Messages\n\n```json\n{ \"type\": \"choose_color\", \"color\": \"white\" }\n{ \"type\": \"choose_color\", \"color\": \"black\" }\n{ \"type\": \"choose_color\", \"color\": \"random\" }\n{ \"type\": \"ready\" }\n{ \"type\": \"unready\" }\n{ \"type\": \"move\", \"move\": { \"type\": \"place\", \"piece\": \"ant\", \"to\": { \"q\": 0, \"r\": 0 } } }\n{ \"type\": \"move\", \"move\": { \"type\": \"move\", \"from\": { \"q\": 0, \"r\": 0 }, \"to\": { \"q\": 1, \"r\": 0 } } }\n{ \"type\": \"move\", \"move\": { \"type\": \"pass\" } }\n{ \"type\": \"resign\" }\n{ \"type\": \"leave\" }\n```\n\nThe legal moves for the current state are sent by the server in the `legalMoves` field (in `match_started`, `match_state` and `move_played`), so one of them can be copied into a `move` message.\n\n### Negative cases\n\n- a token that doesn't exist → the connection is closed with code `4001`\n- connecting after the 30 s window expires → `4003`\n- `move` when it's not your turn → `{ \"type\": \"error\", \"message\": \"Not your turn\" }`\n- an illegal move → `Illegal move`\n- `choose_color` during a match → `Match is in progress`\n- any message from a spectator → `Spectators can only watch`\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000"
    },
    {
      "key": "wsUrl",
      "value": "ws://localhost:3000"
    },
    {
      "key": "roomId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "token1",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "token2",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "token3",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/healthz",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "healthz"
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test(\"200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
              "pm.test(\"status ok\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql(\"ok\"));"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Rooms",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Create room (public)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/rooms",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "rooms"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Creates a room and writes its id into the `roomId` variable.",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"visibility\": \"public\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"201\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"has roomId\", () => pm.expect(body.roomId).to.be.a(\"string\"));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"roomId\", body.roomId);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Create room (private)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/rooms",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "rooms"
              ]
            },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n    \"visibility\": \"private\"\n}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"201\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.test(\"private\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().visibility).to.eql(\"private\"));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "List public rooms",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/rooms",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "rooms"
              ]
            }
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test(\"array\", () => pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.be.an(\"array\"));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Join (player 1)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/join",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "rooms",
                "{{roomId}}",
                "join"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Writes the token into `token1`. Connect over WebSocket within 30 s."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"role player\", () => pm.expect(body.role).to.eql(\"player\"));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"token1\", body.token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Join (player 2)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/join",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "rooms",
                "{{roomId}}",
                "join"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Writes the token into `token2`."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"role player\", () => pm.expect(body.role).to.eql(\"player\"));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"token2\", body.token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "Join (spectator)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/rooms/{{roomId}}/join",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "rooms",
                "{{roomId}}",
                "join"
              ]
            },
            "description": "A third join into a full room gets the spectator role. Writes the token into `token3`."
          },
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"200\", () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test(\"role spectator\", () => pm.expect(body.role).to.eql(\"spectator\"));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set(\"token3\", body.token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
